documentation warns that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140), so a caller with a deadline and retries is not blocked; the source shows the wrapper cannot distinguish this state from that warning's case.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The harness drives a wrapped node against a bare raft instance, so the wrapper's asynchronous ready/advance contract is exercised on one side only, and both nodes run in one process; the leader is installed directly before the removal and the campaign is driven through the wrapper's own Campaign.\\\",\n   \\\"The proposed calls use a 300ms deadline: the receipt measures that the call did not complete within it and that the group's log did not change, not the exact duration of the closed channel.\\\",\n   \\\"The exercised group has two voters; whether a larger group reaches the same state (where the re-added node's Progress entry is recreated in a different position, and the leader that removed it may not be the leader that re-adds it) is not measured.\\\",\n   \\\"Whether an application is expected to keep proposing through a node that has been removed and re-added is itself part of the question; the library's own comment calls the mechanism unsound rather than documenting an intended semantics.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The proposal channel is closed by the removal guard and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"With a nil proposal channel Propose blocks until the caller's context or the node's done channel fires.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@k-propc-close-cases\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"Only a removal closes the channel; a demotion keeps the Progress entry and an addition never re-opens it.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@k-propose-no-distinct-error\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"Propose can only return ctx.Err() or ErrStopped for this state, with no distinct error.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update27.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update27.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"10b3ddfa3d914121bb0b6c1901d393f6\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 3225.543675125009, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": false, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@k-propc-close-cases\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@k-propose-no-distinct-error\"}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"update\", \"target\": \"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"discriminator\"]}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"rationale\", \"knowledge\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update27.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded the source-explained boundaries of the third finding. Two behaviours are now durable: (1) the Node wrapper closes its proposal channel only for the removal case, because the guard requires the local node's Progress entry to disappear while it was present - a demotion to learner keeps that entry and therefore leaves the channel open - and applying a change that adds the node back takes the okBefore=false path, so an addition never re-opens a channel a removal closed, leaving the leadership-change branch (measured in the receipt) as the only repair site; (2) Node.Propose cannot report this state as such: with a nil channel it waits on a select over that channel, the caller's context and the node's done channel, so it returns only ctx.Err() or ErrStopped - the same results an ordinary lost proposal or a stopped node produces - which is why a caller with a deadline cannot tell the closed channel from a lost proposal except through the node's status. The measured account is unchanged and still rests on receipt c53145c01ad94b449ca1c8b81fe8d7b4 with its controls (parsed index 1), premises and violated witness (index 4) and its restore comparisons (indices 5 and 6); counterevidence gained the demotion exclusion and the source point that the wrapper's own warning does not describe this case, and limitations now name the only remaining unmeasured item - whether a group larger than two voters reaches the same state, where a re-added node's Progress entry is recreated in a different position and the leader that removed it may not be the leader that re-adds it - which is also what the question's discriminator now carries. No new execution was requested.\"}"}}
